==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Torte}}. Cognate to {{m|en|tart#Etymology 2|tart}}. {{doublet|en|torta}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/tɔːt/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-tort.ogg|a=RP}}
* {{enPR|tô(ɹ)t|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/tɔɹt/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-tort.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{homophones|en|tort|;|taught|taut<aa:non-rhotic>}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)t|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|torten}}

# A rich, dense [[cake]], typically made with many eggs and relatively little flour (as opposed to a [[sponge cake]] or [[gâteau]]).

